186045417 true] [17592186425716 1072 #uuid "161536f2-53fb-500a-9485-9d3528da9c26" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425716 1074 "In the model, there are $2$ shapes. Each shape consists of $4$ pieces that each represent $\\frac{1}{4}$ of a whole. There are $8$ pieces in total.\n\nThe model tells us that when we divide $2$ wholes into quarters, we will be left with $8$ pieces.\n\nHence, the division problem is\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{1}{4}=8.\n$$" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425717 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425713 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425717 1069 "q-59863" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425717 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425717 1071 "![](images/92/9298eb33dbbe9cfc93712c86370ba589667f9512df85bece397733f85b48a8d7.png)\n\nThe shape in the model above represents $1$ whole. Using this model, find the value of $1÷\\frac{1}{8}.$" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425717 1072 #uuid "1a222c00-c53f-5553-bfce-020d55c30819" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425717 1074 "To calculate $1÷\\frac{1}{8}$, we need to find how many times $\\frac{1}{8}$ fits into a whole. \n\n![](images/5d/5d97a785920930122759fa9eae688ac30244d54728720aff6f5c7dab21d05fc4.png)\n\n  \n\nWe can see that we get $1\\times 8=8$ parts in total. Therefore:\n\n$$\n1÷\\frac{1}{8}=8\n$$" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425718 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425709 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425718 1069 "q-222821" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425718 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425718 1071 "![](images/9e/9e817bf1feef0f3534898ff4ef4a342bb8388bf5ef07b3850f84063344832b5a.png)\n\nIf the $3$ dishes above are divided into eighths, then there will be{{field-1}}\neighths in total." 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425718 1072 #uuid "231d3968-66d3-5c90-96b8-37d607f95d77" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425718 1074 "Since each part is $\\frac{1}{8}$ of a whole, we need to split each of the $3$ dishes (wholes) into $8$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/55/55be423192cc332d4c8d98223eded4ac3bbed40b36694637912e47a415de9de5.png)\n\n \n\nSo, we get $3\\times 8=24$ pieces in total." 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425719 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425711 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425719 1069 "q-222820" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425719 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425719 1071 "![](images/23/235e19c4e3231eb22e6d43ccadcd90c5694077ec4ce562e6c4f188cfff77545f.png)\n\nIf the $3$ pancakes above are divided into ninths, then there will be{{field-1}}\nninths in total." 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425719 1072 #uuid "a1f85c3b-c75a-57c8-b1c6-0955959346d5" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425719 1074 "Since each part is $\\frac{1}{9}$ of a whole, we need to split each of the $3$ pancakes (wholes) into $9$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/6d/6d7e91b7a982a8e5d4f17072484d0315663ae5c5187aefa49e8c756e785d530e.png)\n\n \n\nSo, we get $3\\times 9=27$ pieces in total." 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425720 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425714 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425720 1069 "q-59609" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425720 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425720 1071 "![](images/5b/5b2aab319e386e3ffa85720f9f32b5acb03f6c8f2518c97676ba617bc2d70888.png)\n\nThe model above represents $2$ wholes. Use this model to calculate the value of $2÷\\frac{1}{4}.$" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425720 1072 #uuid "f3cee5cd-3b4b-5a2f-9ea4-2689dbbea9cb" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425720 1074 "To calculate $2÷\\frac{1}{4}$, we need to divide each of $2$ wholes into $4$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/91/9165eae776ebb82d9f9f577cd44b1f780e3ba44d8ff64eed9940ef9a9f943815.png)\n\n \n\nWe get $2\\times 4=8$ pieces in total. \n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{1}{4}=8\n$$" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425721 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425712 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425721 1069 "q-92122" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425721 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425721 1071 "Which model represents the division problem below?\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{1}{4}=8\n$$" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425721 1072 #uuid "fbfb4627-307e-591d-8189-1156ed697734" 13194139534558 17592186045417 true] [17592186425721 1074 "To calculate $2÷\\frac{1}{4}$, we need to divide each of $2$ wholes into $4$ equal parts, as shown below. This gives us the corresponding model for the given division problem.\n\n![](images/22/227e3080de354aa93af71f70747ab31f7673b6e6e9d0591c84dfafcfe56edc56.png)\n\n \n\nWe get $2\\times 4=8$ pieces in total." 13194139534558 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-11b52c3b-ac40-523d-9342-17b5e4b3a392" 17592186425683 "answer-1eae1920-2802-534b-b1da-7b3ecd0b8120" 17592186425684 "answer-2030409d-4de7-5b60-82e1-ea070a92b04d" 17592186425685 "answer-2aba60ca-5c7e-5b3a-ac1d-d7f7624571e6" 17592186425686 "answer-370ac109-9603-5801-8f92-42b44749e7f3" 17592186425687 "answer-4bb15768-3c00-57fc-95bd-2dfb30ab2f07" 17592186425688 "answer-6356133e-89ba-59a8-9a18-18443c69668f" 17592186425689 "answer-6573b2ed-bdd5-50d2-a3a3-b779cc223e8f" 17592186425690 "answer-8430de0e-935d-55e0-b040-0d3e5fe1615b" 17592186425691 "answer-8f04c205-f5b8-533b-a8e9-61d26c5bc4f4" 17592186425692 "answer-a81f729d-2453-5e72-965f-0fe0c5d6bc0a" 17592186425693 "answer-a8f3ad67-64ee-515e-8f56-2665acd0fa5a" 17592186425694 "answer-ac751d31-e89b-51ee-a5ce-e348b133b267" 17592186425695 "answer-b18a24df-3c48-5f74-b5b4-2e60241bb1bc" 17592186425696 "answer-cd3b6376-8e4f-5c46-bf13-517082472202" 17592186425697 "answer-d8ba79f3-0b1a-5215-8fff-a21e8694dfd4" 17592186425698 "answer-e4e6c36e-181